# --- About page: orientation + documentation -------------------------------
# One page: a quick orientation (what the tool does, how to start) followed by
# the reference material (data provenance, citations, methods, credits).
about_page <- div(
  class = "mx-auto my-3",
  style = "max-width: 900px;",
  card(
    id = "hdr-about",
    card_body(markdown(
      "## DE Explorer

Explore a differential-expression analysis interactively - from a whole-cohort
overview down to a single gene. Part of the **Lifescience Shiny Gallery**:
reusable Shiny apps and components for common bioinformatics workflows.

#### What you can do
- **PCA** - see how samples separate.
- **Results table** - browse and filter every gene; select rows to drive the heatmap.
- **Gene detail** - a selected gene's expression across sample groups.
- **Volcano** - effect size vs significance at your chosen thresholds.
- **Heatmap** - expression of the selected genes across samples.
- **Enrichment** - MSigDB Hallmark pathways over-represented among the hits,
  shown as a dot plot and a full table.
- **AI assistant** - an optional bring-your-own-key chat that reads the current
  views and can drive the controls for you.

#### Getting started
On the **Explorer** tab, pick a dataset in the left controls (the lung LUAD vs
LUSC set loads by default), set the fold-change and significance thresholds, then
work down the page. Selecting rows in the Results table drives the Heatmap; its
gene and display controls live under **Heatmap** in the left rail. New here?
Click **Demo** in the top bar for a guided tour, or open the **assistant** on the
right to ask about any view.

### Data
- **TCGA-BRCA** (`de-brca`) - The Cancer Genome Atlas breast-invasive-carcinoma
  cohort: primary tumour vs solid-tissue normal. Counts come from **recount3**,
  which uniformly re-aligns and quantifies public RNA-seq, so samples are
  directly comparable. We fit **DESeq2** and take VST-log2 expression, restricted
  to protein-coding genes. A curated subset (~40 tumour / 20 normal) ships with
  the app for a fast, reproducible demo; the full cohort has >1,000 tumours.
- **TCGA Lung** (`de-lung`, the default) - a **three-group** set: lung adenocarcinoma (LUAD)
  vs squamous-cell carcinoma (LUSC), plus solid-tissue normal, from the TCGA-LUAD
  and TCGA-LUSC cohorts via recount3 → DESeq2 → VST. The DE contrast is the
  tumour-subtype comparison **LUAD vs LUSC**; colour the PCA or gene-detail
  boxplots **by group** to see all three at once.
- **Airway** (`de-airway`) - dexamethasone-treated airway smooth-muscle cells, a
  classic DESeq2 dataset.
- **Synthetic** - a reproducible generator for testing.

Prep scripts under `data/prep/` are the source of truth (provenance + licensing).

#### Citations
- TCGA Network. *Comprehensive molecular portraits of human breast tumours.*
  Nature 490:61–70 (2012). doi:10.1038/nature11412
- TCGA Network. *Comprehensive molecular profiling of lung adenocarcinoma.*
  Nature 511:543–550 (2014). doi:10.1038/nature13385
- TCGA Network. *Comprehensive genomic characterization of squamous cell lung
  cancers.* Nature 489:519–525 (2012). doi:10.1038/nature11404
- Wilks C, et al. *recount3: summaries and queries for large-scale RNA-seq
  expression and splicing.* Genome Biol 22:323 (2021).
  doi:10.1186/s13059-021-02533-6
- Love MI, Huber W, Anders S. *Moderated estimation of fold change and dispersion
  for RNA-seq data with DESeq2.* Genome Biol 15:550 (2014).
  doi:10.1186/s13059-014-0550-8
- Liberzon A, et al. *The Molecular Signatures Database Hallmark gene set
  collection.* Cell Syst 1:417–425 (2015). doi:10.1016/j.cels.2015.12.004
- Himes BE, et al. *RNA-seq transcriptome profiling identifies CRISPLD2 as a
  glucocorticoid responsive gene in human airway smooth muscle cells.* PLoS One
  9:e99625 (2014). doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0099625

TCGA data are subject to the [NIH Genomic Data Sharing Policy](https://gdc.cancer.gov/access-data/data-access-policies);
the processed subset here is derived from open-access recount3 summaries.

### Methods
- **Volcano / table** classify each gene Up / Down / Not-significant from your
  |log2 fold change| and significance thresholds (adjusted or raw *p*).
- **PCA** runs on the most-variable genes.
- **Heatmap** shows per-gene expression, optionally row z-scored and clustered.
- **Enrichment** is hypergeometric over-representation (`stats::phyper`) of the
  significant genes against the MSigDB **Hallmark** collection, drawn as a dot
  plot (gene ratio, overlap size, adjusted *p*) and a table.
- **Multi-group datasets** (e.g. lung) colour the PCA and gene boxplots by group;
  the per-gene test switches to Kruskal-Wallis when there are more than two
  groups. The volcano and table always use one two-group DE contrast.

### Bring your own data
Match the DE data contract - `de_results.csv`, `expression.csv`, `metadata.csv` -
and choose *Upload your own…* in the dataset picker. See the data-contract and
reuse guides under the repository `docs/`.

### Credits
Built with **Shiny** + **bslib**. MIT © 2026 Posit Software, PBC. Authored by Samuel Bharti."
    ))
  )
)

